-- title:
--   Degeneracy map q↦ q^ℓ on complex place dictionaries
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma,\Gamma'\le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ be subgroups each containing $T=\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, let $\ell$ be a nonzero natural number, and suppose $\Gamma'\le$ `CongruenceSubgroup.conjGL` $\Gamma\,(\,$[`ModularForm.heckeDiagMatrix`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperator.html#L21) $\ell)$, the subgroup cut out by conjugation by the matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\ell,1)\in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$ into $\Gamma$. Let $F_0,F_1$ be intermediate fields of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\mathbb Q((q))$ and write $\mathbb C F_i=$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) $\mathbb C\,F_i$ for the $\mathbb C$-subfield of $\mathbb C((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $F_i$. Let $D$ be a complex place dictionary for $(\Gamma,F_0)$ and $D'$ one for $(\Gamma',F_1)$: each assigns to every $\tau\in\mathfrak H$ a place of the relevant function field over $\mathbb C$ and a positive integer `ramification` $\tau$, the places being invariant under the respective group, membership in the valuation ring of the place at $\tau$ being equivalent to local boundedness near $\tau$ of the realisation `realizeOf`, and the meromorphic order at $\tau$ of that realisation being `ramification` $\tau$ times the order of the element at the place. Let $\beta\colon \mathbb C F_0\to\mathbb C F_1$ be a $\mathbb C$-algebra homomorphism which on underlying Laurent series is the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ ([`ModularCurve.qExpand`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) $\mathbb C\,\ell$, the shift of exponents by multiplication by $\ell$), and assume $\beta$ integral. Then for every $\tau\in\mathfrak H$ the restriction along $\beta$ of $D'.\mathrm{pt}\,\tau$ — the place of $\mathbb C F_0$ whose valuation ring is the $\beta$-preimage of that of $D'.\mathrm{pt}\,\tau$ — equals $D.\mathrm{pt}(\mathrm{diag}(\ell,1)\cdot\tau)$, i.e. the place attached to $\ell\tau$, and $D'.\mathrm{ramification}\,\tau$ times the ramification index of $D'.\mathrm{pt}\,\tau$ along $\beta$ (the least positive $n$ of the form $\mathrm{ord}_{D'.\mathrm{pt}\,\tau}(\beta f)$ with $0\ne f\in\mathbb C F_0$) equals $D.\mathrm{ramification}(\ell\tau)$.
--
--   This is the description on points, with multiplicities, of the degeneracy map $\tau\mapsto \ell\tau$ from the modular curve of level $\Gamma'$ to that of level $\Gamma$, which on $q$-expansions is the operator $x(q)\mapsto x(q^{\ell})$: the point of $\tau$ goes to the point of $\ell\tau$, and the local ramification indices multiply as $e_{\Gamma'}(\tau)\cdot e_\beta(\tau)=e_\Gamma(\ell\tau)$. It is used in the computation of the divisor of the Hecke correspondence, in [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.heckeDivHBar_single_pt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.heckeDivHBar_single_pt).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf_restrictAlong_pt_qExpand.lean

